{"name":"Sweet Alyssum","hex":"#e7c2de","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet alyssum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A low-growing flowering annual (Lobularia maritima)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_alyssum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Alyssum (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Alyssum is a 1915 American silent drama film directed by Colin Campbell and starring Tyrone Power Sr., Kathlyn Williams, and Edith Johnson. A print of Sweet Alyssum exists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Alyssum_(film)"},{"title":"Lobularia maritima","blocks":[{"text":"Lobularia maritima is a species of low-growing flowering plant in the family Brassicaceae. Its common name is sweet alyssum or sweet Alison, also commonly referred to as just alyssum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Smagliczka_nadmorska_1.jpg/330px-Smagliczka_nadmorska_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lobularia_maritima"},{"title":"Alyssum","blocks":[{"text":"Alyssum is a genus of over a hundred species of flowering plants in the family Brassicaceae, native to temperate Europe, Asia, and northern Africa, with the highest species diversity in the Mediterranean region. The genus comprises annual and perennial herbaceous plants or (rarely) small shrubs, growing to 10–100 cm tall, with oblong-oval leaves. Alyssum flowers are characteristically small and grouped in terminal clusters; they are often yellow or white colored but can be pink or purple."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Alyssum_montanum_ENBLA06.jpg/330px-Alyssum_montanum_ENBLA06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alyssum"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Sweet_Alyssum_%28film%29.jpg/500px-Sweet_Alyssum_%28film%29.jpg?utm_